---
description: ProjectWise QC workflow debugging
alwaysApply: true
---

When investigating ProjectWise workflow behavior, QC automation, notifications, state transitions, audit events, package status, or workflow drift:

1. Use available ProjectWise/QC MCP tools before inspecting code.
2. Gather evidence from MCP tools.
3. Identify where the workflow chain breaks.
4. Only then inspect source code.
5. Do not propose fixes without supporting MCP evidence.

When debugging job enqueue/run/fail/lock/stale/duplicate issues, inspect the live queue/log share first via Show-QCQueueDiag. Then use pw-qc-debug MCP to validate SQL, ProjectWise, audit, notifications, and package integrity.
